    "_id": "post_292",
    "post_type": "discussion",
    "author_id": "usr_4",
    "title": "TypeScript 5.6 Released with Disallowed Nullish Checks and Iterator Helper Methods",
    "content": "Microsoft Developer Tools has announced the general availability of TypeScript 5.6.\n\n### Key Highlights\n- **Disallowed Nullish and Truthy Checks**: Syntax errors are now raised when syntax patterns like `if (/regex/)` or `x => true` are erroneously used where expressions are always truthy.\n- **Iterator Helpers Support**: Types and method definitions for standard ECMAScript Iterator methods (`map`, `filter`, `take`, `drop`, `flatMap`).\n- **Project Reference Speedups**: Substantial reductions in memory usage and parsing latency for large monorepos building in `--build` mode.\n\nSource: Microsoft TypeScript Official Blog by Daniel Rosenwasser.",
    "community_id": "comm_frontend",
    "community_slug": "frontend",
    "flair": "Tooling News",
    "tags": [
      "typescript",
      "frontend",
      "developer-tools"
    ],
