    "_id": "post_305",
    "post_type": "discussion",
    "author_id": "usr_11",
    "title": "Comparing io_uring SQPOLL mode with epoll for millions of concurrent WebSocket connections",
    "content": "Linux io_uring offers a kernel submission polling mode (IORING_SETUP_SQPOLL) where a dedicated kernel thread polls the submission queue ring buffer continuously.\n\nThis eliminates user-space syscall overhead during high-frequency I/O loops.\n\nHowever, the tradeoff is significant: the polling thread pins an entire CPU core at 100% busy-waiting unless tuned with `sq_thread_idle` sleep timeouts. For steady high-throughput network services it is a huge win, but for spiky workloads standard epoll is still much more power-efficient.",
    "community_id": "comm_linux",
