    "_id": "post_306",
    "post_type": "discussion",
    "author_id": "usr_48",
    "title": "eBPF XDP packet filtering: dropping DDoS amplification attacks at line rate on 100GbE Mellanox NICs",
    "content": "When an authoritative DNS server encounters reflection floods, user-space sockets and even iptables connection tracking collapse under softirq processing overhead.\n\nBy attaching an eBPF program to the driver layer of the network card using eXpress Data Path (XDP_DRV mode), invalid DNS query packets are parsed and returned with `XDP_DROP` before the kernel allocates an `sk_buff` structure.\n\nIt's night and day compared to filtering higher up in the network stack: the host remains responsive without dropping legitimate SSH or control plane traffic.",
    "community_id": "comm_linux",
