    "post_type": "discussion",
    "author_id": "usr_33",
    "title": "Why we replaced distributed locks with causal version vectors in multi-region edge architectures",
    "content": "Running Redis distributed locks across multi-region edge nodes introduced unavoidable round-trip delays on every state mutation.\n\nDuring network blips, lock lease timeouts caused cascading split-brain panics in our inventory service.\n\nWe transitioned to dotted version vectors with deterministic conflict resolution (last-write-wins with logical timestamp tie-breakers for commutative operations). Writes now complete locally at the edge, and state converges asynchronously over cross-region streams.",
    "community_id": "comm_systems",
    "community_slug": "systems",
    "flair": "Distributed Systems",
