    "_id": "post_309",
    "post_type": "discussion",
    "author_id": "usr_35",
    "title": "FP8 post-training quantization: balancing perplexity and matrix multiplication speed on Hopper Tensor Cores",
    "content": "Nvidia Hopper H100 tensor cores introduce native FP8 execution (E4M3 for weights/activations, E5M2 for gradients), offering double the raw TFLOPS of FP16.\n\nHowever, naive per-tensor quantization introduces severe accuracy degradation on attention logits due to outlier activations in deeper transformer layers.\n\nUtilizing per-channel scaling factors for weights combined with smooth-quantization to migrate outlier scales from activations into weights preserves model accuracy on reasoning tasks while keeping inference latency fast.",
