    "post_type": "discussion",
    "author_id": "usr_6",
    "title": "WebGPU compute shaders for 100,000 particle N-body gravitational simulations running at 120fps",
    "content": "Running gravitational N-body simulations in JavaScript on the CPU slows to a crawl with just 2,000 particles due to O(N^2) pair-wise force calculations.\n\nBy offloading the computation to a WebGPU compute shader with SharedArrayBuffer workgroup memory (`var<workgroup> tile: array<vec4<f32>, 256>`), each thread in a 256-thread workgroup cooperatively loads particle positions into ultra-fast on-chip GPU shared memory.\n\nThe simulation effortlessly calculates gravitation for 100,000 particles at a rock-solid 120fps on an Apple M2 Max, leaving the CPU completely idle.",
