    "author_id": "usr_106",
    "title": "Full acoustic guitar setup: bone saddle sanding, fret crowning, and fresh phosphor bronze strings",
    "content": "My parlor acoustic had developed slight fret buzz on the 4th fret and the action at the 12th fret felt overly stiff.\n- Measured neck relief with a notched straightedge and adjusted the double-action truss rod 1/8th turn clockwise.\n- Sanded 0.6mm off the bottom of the compensated unbleached bone saddle on 320-grit sandpaper over a flat granite slab.\n- Strung up with D'Addario 12-53 phosphor bronze strings. Action is now a comfortable 2.1mm on the low E with zero rattle.",
    "community_id": "comm_music",
    "community_slug": "music-production",
