    "title": "Designing and assembling an autonomous rover flight controller PCB: SMD reflow and bench validation",
    "content": "Our university robotics team needed a custom sensor telemetry board combining an STM32H7 microcontroller, dual IMUs, and CAN transceiver.\n- Hand-placed 0603 passive components and QFN chips using tweezers under a stereo inspection microscope.\n- Reflowed on a low-cost temperature-controlled hot plate with lead-free solder paste.\n- Flashed custom Zephyr RTOS firmware and verified all SPI bus transactions without a single dropped packet!",
    "community_id": "comm_campus",
    "community_slug": "campus-life",
    "flair": "Robotics PCB",
